every month thousands of people arrive  in the EU seeking asylum in 2016 alone  1.3 million people applied for asylum in  the EU which is actually a decrease on  the year before but it is still a large  burden for countries like Italy and  Greece where migrants arrive first the  European Asylum support office is based  in Malta established in 2010 it  coordinates asylum procedures throughout  Europe the main idea of the European  Asylum Agency is that we have to work  together that the European solution that  is what we need not a member state  solutions but we need one common  European solution this means training  country officials about asylum laws  facilitating the flow of information and  data across borders or working with  Europe's courts and tribunals to  regulate asylum law across the block the  office is there to help in refugee  hotspots those places that receive a  steady flow of migrants for instance the  agency deploy support workers on the  ground to help people who have just  arrived and identifies vulnerable people  like unaccompanied minors and provides  them with the support they need in 2016  there were more than 65,000  unaccompanied minors who applied for  asylum in the EU armed with data like  this the agency is able to coordinate  and help the people who need it most
 

